# Build context of Dockerfile.test (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# instead of .dockerignore). Unlike the runtime image, the test image needs
# tests/, fixtures/ and the web sources; it still never gets secrets or the
# host's toolchains (a Windows .venv or node_modules would not run on Linux).

# Secrets and local config.
.env
.env.*

# Host toolchains and build output (the image installs its own).
.venv/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
app/static/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Not needed to run the tests. (.github/ stays in: the unit tests read
# .github/workflows/promote-prod.yml; workflow files hold no secret.)
.git/
.claude/
.agents/
_docs/*
# ...except the redaction contract, which tests/unit/test_agent_tool_results.py
# checks against agent_tools (the drift check of CIW-08.2).
!_docs/api.md
data/
*.log
